            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Usually a blunt or wrong bit, hammer mode not actually engaged, too little forward pressure, or you have hit rebar. A hammer drill also struggles in hard, aggregate-rich concrete, which is exactly the point at which a rotary hammer becomes necessary.",
          },
